  - id: contentions_among_you
    displayName: Contentions Among You
    flavorText: Paul rebukes the Corinthians for splitting into factions around Paul,
      Apollos, and Cephas, insisting the apostles are only servants and stewards,
      not figures to be exalted.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Addresses the report that the Corinthian church had split into rival
      factions around Paul, Apollos, Cephas, and Christ; reframes the apostles as
      mere servants and stewards of God's mysteries rather than figures to be exalted
      over one another.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul
    managerId: church_divisions
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 28.304233215207116
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
